-- monster_drops.lua contains bundled reference data. See its schema below and CODE_GUIDE.md.
-- Used by: drop_menu.lua, map_hover.lua, nearby_npcs.lua, reference_pins.lua.
--[=[
BEGINNER WALKTHROUGH: monster_drops.lua

This is a DICTIONARY keyed by exact catalogue monster name, not an indexed list.
Each named block contains level (display text), drops (ordered rows), source (Wiki URL),
retrieved (date), and revision where available. Each drop has name, quantity and rarity
text; conditions/variants mean these strings are not unconditional probabilities.

Example reuse:
  local monsters = require('monster_drops')
  local info = monsters['Abyssal beast']
  if info then
      print(info.level, info.source)
      for _, drop in ipairs(info.drops) do print(drop.name, drop.quantity, drop.rarity) end
  end
map_hover.lua builds popup slots from these rows; drop_menu.lua checks record availability.
drop_item_ids.lua is a separate artwork lookup keyed by each drop.name.
Use pairs to visit all named records; ipairs/# do not enumerate a string-keyed dictionary.
Keep provenance and attribution when adapting the data; see WIKI-NPCS.md.

Cross-file connections:
  No require dependencies inside this file.
  Required directly by: drop_menu.lua, map_hover.lua.

require normally caches a module after the first load. A data module returns values;
a helper module returns functions/state constructors. See CODE_GUIDE.md for the full flow.
]=]

--[[
Bundled Wiki-derived monster-drop reference, keyed by catalogue monster name.
Each value contains level, drops and source/retrieval provenance. Drops hold item names,
quantity and rarity text; variant-specific conditions may not be completely represented.
No live loot tracking, probability calculation or runtime Wiki request is performed.
Keep provenance alongside entries and preserve names used by drop_menu/map_hover.
Source/license/retrieval details: WIKI-NPCS.md (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0).
]]

